@c APPENDICES
@node Version History
@appendix Version History

@table @dfn
@item Version 0.8.0, November 21, 2026
@itemize
@item
New @code{stats} command, which measures a tree and writes it as a
@dfn{Statistics} chapter: lines of code, of comment and of nothing, the
decision points the code holds, how much of the exported API is
documented, and, from the repository's history, the authors and the churn.
@item
This manual's own Statistics chapter is that command's output: it is
generated by @code{maak docs} and taken again by @code{maak release}, and
it names the commit it describes.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.7.0, November 21, 2026
@itemize
@item
Mermaid diagrams: a fenced block in a docstring or a commentary is drawn
and shown in the manual, or written as source when no renderer is at
hand. New @code{--mermaid-command} option.
@item
New @code{check} command, which reports the exported names that have no
documentation string and exits non-zero when it found one.
@item
Every definition carries an anchor, so a chapter written by hand can
@code{@@ref} a single procedure.
@item
The API chapter opens with the list of modules it documents, each one a
link to its section.
@item
An @code{@@image} or an @code{@@itemize} no longer runs into the text
that follows it.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.6.2, November 17, 2026
@itemize
@item
Every definition is documented in Texinfo, and the API reference is
regenerated from those docstrings.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.6.1, November 17, 2026
@itemize
@item
Rebranded: a new icon, wordmark and project page, so the whole tree is
under the MIT license.
@item
Fixed the CI gates: the manifest names its packages, and the @code{check}
task runs its whole script.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.6.0, November 17, 2026
@itemize
@item
The project was renamed from Guile Documentá to Guile Dokgen: the
program is now @command{dokgen} and the modules are @code{(dokgen @dots{})}.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.5.0, November 17, 2026
@itemize
@item
Hard fork under new maintainership. The license changed from the
public domain to the MIT license, and every source file now carries an
SPDX license header.
@item
The project layout, the build recipes (a Maak file and a pinned Guix
channel set for @command{guix time-machine}) and the contribution
practices follow those of @command{sift}.
@item
The sources moved to @file{src/}, and the launcher to @file{bin/dokgen}.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.4.0, July 05, 2025
@itemize
@item
@code{api} command: The @code{source} argument is now called
@code{sources} and accepts one or more paths to Guile Scheme
modules or Guile Scheme directories. For example:

@example
$ dokgen api libx.scm
$ dokgen api liby
$ dokgen api "libz.scm libz"
@end example

@item
@code{api} command: The @code{destination} argument, which was a
positional argument, became a keyword argument called
@code{--destination}, and abbreviated as @code{-d}.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.3.0, June 22, 2025
@itemize
@item
Macros are now documented with name, arguments and documentation
strings instead of simply copied verbatim to the exported
documentation.
@item
Added support to document parameter objects. Module documentation
sections now include a "Parameters" subsection if they export
parameters. The parameters are also listed in the "Variable Index".
@end itemize

@item Version 0.2.1, Oct 16, 2023
@itemize
@item
Enable installing Guile Dokgen from the package provided by my
personal Guix Channel X. Two unit tests that pass in Guile Dokgen's
development environment (which uses Guix shell) were failing when
building the package with Guix. Both tests were marked as expected
fails to make the test suite pass regardless of the issues and be able
to install the package successfully. This is a temporary fix until the
origin of the issues is found.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.2.0, May 31, 2023
@itemize
@item
Rename @command{extract} command to @command{api} so that it is
easier to separate API documentation and CLI documentation extraction.
@item
Add project website.
@end itemize

@item Version 0.1.0, April 13, 2023
@itemize
@item
Initial release of the software providing a program to generate API
documentation of Guile Scheme libraries in Texinfo format.
@end itemize
